---
description: React/Next.js/Tailwind UI conventions
globs: ["app/**/*.tsx", "components/**/*.tsx"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Mobile-first: design for ~375px width first, then scale up with sm:/md:/lg:.
- Use shadcn/ui components; don't hand-roll inputs/buttons/dialogs.
- Server Components by default; add "use client" only when interactivity needs it.
- Big tap targets (min 44px). Clear primary action per screen.
- Every screen: loading, empty, and error states.
- The customer quote page (/q/[token]) must look premium and load fast — it's what
  wins the job. No layout shift, works great on a phone.
- Keep secret keys and server logic out of client components.
